{
  "id": "DrugBank_DB00694 - MONDO_19457",
  "verbalization": "Daunorubicin is associated with the therapy-related acute myeloid leukemia and myelodysplastic syndrome through a chain of indications that connect it to ivosidenib and decitabine. The final scores from the three paths indicate a strong, consistent relationship, suggesting that Daunorubicin may be repurposed for this condition. The evidence suggests that Daunorubicin, through its indication for unclassified acute myeloid leukemia, is linked to ivosidenib, which in turn is linked to therapy-related acute myeloid leukemia and myelodysplastic syndrome. Decitabine, another drug indicated for unclassified acute myeloid leukemia, also shows a similar pathway to the target condition. This suggests that Daunorubicin may be used in combination with other drugs like ivosidenib and decitabine to treat this condition. The evidence supports a potential repurposing of Daunorubicin, but further clinical studies are needed to confirm its efficacy and safety in this context.",
